-All templates select documented versions, but full REST create/GET response contracts for auxiliary deployment resources are not established by these bounded template excerpts. No unsupported feature is silently selected: resource type versions must be explicitly present in future Bicep, warnings/unknown fields resolved before deploying; unsupported log table settings remain listed deployment prerequisites. No metric alert is selected; adding one requires an evidenced Microsoft.Insights/metricAlerts version and revised contract.
+The selected-version documented REST create/GET response contracts for all sixteen auxiliary deployment resource types are retained in [auxiliary-response-contracts.md](provider/task5-fix1/auxiliary-response-contracts.md), with method/path, status/body model, resource envelope and defined async headers. Every auxiliary GET reads its exact PUT resource path with the same selected api-version; Storage account read is the get-properties operation. Successful response models are single resource objects, not value collections. For example, RoleDefinition PUT documents201 (not200), StorageAccount PUT documents200/202, and LogTable PUT documents200/202 with Azure-AsyncOperation. Official relocated publisher Swagger supplies ActionGroup2023-01-01 and ScheduledQueryRule2023-12-01 responses where Learn REST pages failed; exact failures remain retained. Actual responses, provisioning completion, build/type validation and effective readback remain Stage7. StorageAccount GET schema says Standard_ZRS primaryEndpoints returns only Blob endpoint; lack of Table endpoint in that envelope is not evidence that Tables is unsupported, and the exact selected Table HTTPS route must be verified independently. No unsupported feature is silently selected: future Bicep must explicitly contain these versions and resolve warnings/unknown fields before deployment. No metric alert is selected; adding one requires an evidenced Microsoft.Insights/metricAlerts version and revised contract.
 
 ## Selected data-plane contracts and Task 4 compatibility boundary
 
 Blob SDK `azure-storage-blob 12.31.0` supports explicit `api_version="2026-04-06"`, selected for every Blob client, including ADF GET `x-ms-version`. The tagged publisher `_serialize.py` supports it; `_shared/constants.py` chooses the last supported version by default (`2026-10-06`). Explicit version pin avoids that mutable/default discrepancy. Microsoft Storage versioning documents `2026-04-06` fully deployed, with newer versions enabled in the candidate US regions; documentation remains distinct from actual account proof. Tables SDK `azure-data-tables 12.7.0` supports `2019-02-02`, `2019-07-07`, `2020-12-06`; select explicit `api_version="2020-12-06"`. Tagged `_base_client.py` documents default 2019-02-02, so this pin is intentional. Publisher source/tag observations are not actual installed request traces. [Blob source](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/Azure/azure-sdk-for-python/azure-storage-blob_12.31.0/sdk/storage/azure-storage-blob/azure/storage/blob/_serialize.py), [Tables source](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/Azure/azure-sdk-for-python/azure-data-tables_12.7.0/sdk/tables/azure-data-tables/azure/data/tables/_base_client.py), [Storage versions](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/rest/api/storageservices/versioning-for-the-azure-storage-services).
 
 | Data object / lifecycle | API selection, method/path and response requirement | Safeguard / limitation |
 |---|---|---|
 | Raw snapshots, observations, worksets, result reports, quarantine, generation Parquet, manifests, approval evidence | Blob only: PUT `https://{account}.blob.core.windows.net/{container}/{path}` (Put Blob); large BlockBlob upload uses PUT `?comp=block&blockid=...` then PUT `?comp=blocklist`; GET/HEAD same object for bytes/properties; responses/ETag/content hash retained by later implementation | New immutable paths/create-if-absent; verify exact final bytes/hash before manifest/approval/pointer. Never create these via DFS Path Create, NFS or portal tooling that changes the write API. No append/page blobs, DFS rename or recursive directory deletion dependency. |
 | Lock sentinel | Blob-created block blob; PUT `?comp=lease` acquire/renew/release/break (operator recovery only), GET/HEAD properties; lease ID in required leased writes | Lease excludes writes/deletes to that blob, not network traffic or Table writes. Parent lease-loss stop, bounded in-flight requests and takeover checks retained. |
 | Source/attempt/active-pointer/approval entity | Table GET `{table}(PartitionKey='...',RowKey='...')`; POST `{table}` insert; PUT or MERGE exact entity with actual opaque ETag in If-Match for replace/merge | Conditional update 204, mismatch 412; no wildcard `*`, missing If-Match or upsert as CAS. First insert conflicts must be reconciled. No atomic Blob+Table transaction assumed. |

